[00:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hello. Today we\'re going to unbox a Steam Machine. Do a quick overview of the features, and show you how to get started playing games. This is what the box looks like for a two terabyte Steam Machine with Steam Controller bundle. If you got a different model'

[00:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your box will probably come with less stuff inside. The Steam Controller is under here. These boxes contain two extra faceplates that come with the two terabyte Steam Machine, both the standalone and bundle models. We\'ll take a look at those in a bit.'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And here\'s the Steam Machine. You can pull it out of the box using the attached handle. The standalone Steam Machine model comes in the same box. Pull this tab to unseal it, then flip the lid back to open.'

[00:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Ta-da! Inside the box is a Steam Machine, an HDMI cable, and a power cord that matches your region\'s power outlets. Let\'s take a look at Steam Machine.'

[00:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s about six inches square, around the size of a tissue box or these other tissue box sized things. Steam Machine comes with all the ports you need for a living room or desktop setup. On the front, there\'s two USB-A ports, a microSD slot,'

[01:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'An LED strip, an indicator LED, and the power button. On the back, you have DisplayPort, HDMI, power, Gigabit Ethernet, a USB-C port, and two USB-A ports.'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Inside Steam Machine, you have dedicated Wi-Fi and Bluetooth antennas designed to avoid interference. In addition, there is a built in Steam Controller wireless adapter, which lets you pair your Steam Controller'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'directly to your Steam Machine without using the Steam Controller puck. Steam Machine’s power supply is also inside the chassis, so no need to hide a power brick when managing your cables. The front faceplate is removable on all Steam Machine models.'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you have the two terabyte model, it comes with two extra faceplates for customization. One is solid walnut and the other is covered in bright red fabric. We\'ll be releasing the CAD files and details for these faceplates soon,'

[02:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and we\'re excited to see what the community creates. Getting started with Steam Machine is as simple as plugging it into power and connecting it to your display with the included HDMI cord.'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You can also use DisplayPort if you prefer, or even both at the same time. One quick note about Steam Machine placement. Please make sure Steam Machine is not directly on carpet or in an enclosed space.'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The cooling system brings in air through the bottom vent and out the back, so make sure your Steam Machine has room to breathe. Press the power button to turn it on and you\'ll see initial setup instructions on your screen. If you got the Steam Controller bundle or already own a Steam Controller,'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'plug your puck into Steam Machine and turn on your Steam Controller. Follow the on screen prompts to complete any necessary updates. When you\'re done updating, you\'ll be prompted to pair directly'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to the Steam Machine. We think this is a great way to use Steam Machine with Steam Controller, and allows you to do things like turn on the Steam Machine from the controller. Just like the Steam Controller puck, you can pair up to four Steam Controllers to Steam Machine’s internal adapter.'

[03:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'When you pair this way, the Steam Controller puck is no longer used for wireless connectivity, but it\'s still a great way to charge your Steam Controller. For instance,'

[03:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you could have the puck plugged in on a side table next to your couch for quick pick up and play. You\'re also welcome to use a different controller or mouse and keyboard. Steam Machine supports every controller Steam does, so bring whatever input you\'re the most comfortable with.'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Plug your input of choice into Steam Machine via USB and make your way through the rest of the setup experience. You\'ll be able to pair your controller directly via Bluetooth later as well. Once you log in, you\'ll see a familiar UI.'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you\'ve ever used Big Picture Mode or a Steam Deck. Your whole Steam library will be there. Steam Machine run SteamOS just like Steam Deck, and you can expect the same easy to use gamepad-first user interface, integrated system updates,'

[03:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and all the quality of life features you know from Steam Deck. You\'ll also have access to desktop mode, just like any SteamOS device. Managing, purchasing, and launching games is simple with the gamepad-first UI.'

[04:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In addition, Steam Machine has a Verified Program similar to Steam Deck, so you\'ll know at a glance if a game is verified, playable, unsupported, or untested on Steam Machine. With six times the horsepower of the Steam Deck, we\'ve found that many games'

[04:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that were unsupported or just playable on Steam Deck play great and are verified on Steam Machine. In addition to customizing your face plate, you can customize your Steam Machines LED behavior and colors.'

[04:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Or just turn it off. And just like Steam Deck, you can choose your start up movies or change your keyboard styles. You can even have the LED strip show your download progress while installing new games or updates.'

[04:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'When you\'re done playing, just put Steam Machine to sleep from your controller or by pressing the power button. And to learn more about Steam Machine, visit this link.'
